<!-- C#-producer roundtrip PRODUCER: a PLAIN C# class library (Microsoft.NET.Sdk, net10.0) compiling the injected
     .NET runtime source of each migrated CLR-interop `cases/il-*` case (the former per-case runtime.cs). It is
     consumed AS A FAÇADE-FREE .NET LIBRARY by ../consumer through a <ProjectReference>: MSBuild builds this csproj
     first, its implementation dll lands on the consumer's @(ReferencePath)+@(ReferenceCopyLocalPaths), and the
     DotKt pipeline's facadegen (`import <Ns>.<Type>` scan) / bir2cir / ilemit all resolve against it — mechanically
     identical to the former per-case compiler runner's il_check_inject building runtime.cs to a dll and passing it as both a
     compile-ref and a runtime reference (docs/nunit-migration-playbook.md §3).

     Each .cs here is one migrated case's runtime, given its OWN namespace so the many colliding simple names
     (Item/Bag/Sink from clrasm/clriface/geninj) coexist in this single producer assembly — the same per-package
     split the DotKt roundtrip producer uses. This is a plain csc-emitted assembly (no DotKt.Metadata / no retarget);
     the round-trip is "consume a separately-compiled .NET dll AS façade-free Kotlin", the very cross-module shape
     these cases exist to prove. Nullable DISABLED (oblivious): required by Extlib.cs (ktproj-extlib) — its reference-
     type property must surface as the Kotlin PLATFORM type String! (ConeFlexibleType), which only an oblivious/
     non-NRT assembly produces; the other cases carry no NRT-dependent surface. -->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
